\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"f051b52bdf79c3ced16bbd08d9754376c576398b199c30deade5e213307d18bc","event_uuid":"4ef01096-5dee-42d3-99f4-d1d85265c7da","position":{"commit_sha":"91345e9991b6c7e17e57313cc625fa67b9448776","position":"1795088220273932691-4ef01096-5dee-42d3-99f4-d1d85265c7da"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Confirmation by hash, from the sweeps of runs 44487190183 and 44503581058: the Windows result `550e37cbee00c5f27e69148954b33e5b7ddb57f0` is exactly the git blob hash of `caf\u00e9 \u2713\\r\\n`, and the expected `6b2b281e1146f9673f218f9c76042db37be95d03` is the hash of `caf\u00e9 \u2713\\n` (computed locally as sha1 over `blob <len>\\0<bytes>`). So the only difference is newline translation in text-mode stdin; the UTF-8 encoding is right. The source is 04e175d70eb (livid-painful-mosquito, closed), not the A1 stack. A duplicate filed by mistake (metalled-oceangoing-antlion) has been closed against this ticket.","timestamp":1795087532857129675}],"created_at":1795087216133698753,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e25a6468-64e4-4046-b8d6-760ea1fe6678","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"39d8-253b-8d41-4f88"},{"link_uuid":"67c1dd82-d36d-451b-9507-6ad33fc01e3e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e816-b30a-6a5c-4ae4"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from livid-painful-mosquito, whose regression test `tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py::test_run_git_encodes_str_stdin_as_utf8` (both `[subprocess-run]` and `[process-group]`) fails in `sweep (windows)` job 135490319213 (run 44503581058, main at 92d3f373e2c): `assert \"'550e37cbee0...3e5b7ddb57f0'\" == \"'6b2b281e114...2db37be95d03'\"`. This is a new red entry in the advisory Windows sweep, which is held green so that a red result means a new regression.\n\nRoot cause: the test writes `input_data=\"caf\u00e9 \u2713\\n\"` through `run_git` in text mode and compares the blob id with `git hash-object` over the LF-only UTF-8 bytes. On Windows, text-mode `subprocess` stdin translates `\\n` into `\\r\\n` (`io.TextIOWrapper` with the default `newline=None` writes `os.linesep`), so git hashes `caf\u00e9 \u2713\\r\\n`. The test's expectation is wrong; the encoding under test (UTF-8) is correct. The subject-decoding cases pass on Windows.\n\n## Approach\n\nSend stdin with no line ending: `input_data=\"caf\u00e9 \u2713\"`, and compute the expected id over `\"caf\u00e9 \u2713\".encode(\"utf-8\")`. That isolates the property under test (the codec) from the newline translation, which is platform behaviour of text mode and not this test's concern. No product code changes; no config key, env var or flag. Portable: the test then has no line-ending dependence.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py`: the stdin case's input and expectation.\n\n## Testing\n\n`pytest tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py` passes on macOS (6 tests). A `sweep (windows)` run on main after the merge shows neither stdin case in its failures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py` passes, and `make verify` passes.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] A `sweep (windows)` job on main after the merge does not list `test_run_git_encodes_str_stdin_as_utf8` among its failures. Evidence: run id and job id in a ticket comment.\n  provenance: environment=GitHub Actions windows-latest runner (navapbc/rebar test.yml); principal=workflow_dispatch by the session's gh credential; privilege_posture=read-only CI run; instrument=gh run view --job <id> --log \u2014 only the Windows sweep runs the test on Windows.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py","reason":"send stdin without a line ending so the codec, not newline translation, is tested"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e816-b30a-6a5c-4ae4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"85b673fa-21af-48ab-91cb-daa07c62f9ca","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"3e8c-b2fc-d34e-4a36","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_run_git_encodes_str_stdin_as_utf8 fails on Windows: text-mode stdin turns LF into CRLF","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["60327b71-4a82-4b93-84a6-2d7dc2ac48ef","e25a6468-64e4-4046-b8d6-760ea1fe6678","4254ad2c-549c-496c-ac20-1e065c314822","67c1dd82-d36d-451b-9507-6ad33fc01e3e","08eebcbe-cec7-48db-bcb1-9d29da7a15e0","8f12923b-5f3f-4d5f-bbcf-4a0385769943","85b673fa-21af-48ab-91cb-daa07c62f9ca","4ef01096-5dee-42d3-99f4-d1d85265c7da"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795088220273932692,"uuid":"4062ba83-7fa9-46ee-ba43-0d43f000010f"}
